  "text": "### Bulletin #2: GDPR SAR Updates – New Timelines  \n**Date Issued:** 2026-01-25\n**Effective:** Immediate\n**Audience:** All Staff (especially Operations)  \n**Summary:**\nICO (UK data protection regulator) clarified Subject Access Request (SAR) handling procedures. We must respond to SARs within 30 days, not 60. No extensions allowed unless request is complex.  \n**Key Changes:**\n1. **Response Deadline:** 30 days (not 60) from request date\n2. **Extensions:** Only if request is complex; must explain why to customer\n3. **Format:** Must provide data in electronic format (CSV, PDF, etc.)\n4. **Fees:** Cannot charge unless request \"clearly unfounded\"  \n**Your Responsibility:**\n- If customer requests their personal data, log immediately\n- Assign to Operations Manager\n- Operations Manager: Compile data within 30 days\n- Get Compliance approval before sending to customer  \n**Timeline:**\n- Day 1: Customer requests SAR (email, phone, or form)\n- Day 2: Log in system + send receipt to customer\n- Day 25: Send draft to Compliance for review\n- Day 30: Send to customer (latest)  \n**Questions:** Email dpo@firstuk.bank  \n---",
  "name": "Chunk 4/13",
